1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,535
The lords of the Maya underworld
invited two brothers to a ball game.

2
00:00:04,535 --> 00:00:07,208
It was a trap, and the brothers knew it.

3
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:09,011
It was how their father had died.

4
00:00:09,011 --> 00:00:13,262
The father, Hun Hunahpu, and his
brother played ball so loudly

5
00:00:13,262 --> 00:00:17,547
that the lords of Xibalba, the
underworld, heard it overhead.

6
00:00:17,547 --> 00:00:19,658
They sent owls with an invitation.

7
00:00:19,666 --> 00:00:22,903
The brothers crossed the
rivers of blood and went down.

8
00:00:22,903 --> 00:00:25,853
The lords had set wooden
figures in the seats of honor,

9
00:00:25,853 --> 00:00:27,388
and the brothers greeted them.

10
00:00:27,388 --> 00:00:29,403
Then the lords laughed.

11
00:00:29,474 --> 00:00:31,621
They offered the brothers
a bench to sit on.

12
00:00:31,621 --> 00:00:33,247
It was a burning stone.

13
00:00:33,247 --> 00:00:36,806
They locked them in the House of
Darkness with a torch and a cigar each,

14
00:00:36,806 --> 00:00:39,744
and demanded them back unburned.

15
00:00:40,345 --> 00:00:42,682
By morning, both had burned down.

16
00:00:42,682 --> 00:00:46,213
The brothers were sacrificed,
and buried in the ballcourt.

17
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:50,678
Hun Hunahpu's head was hung in a tree,
and the tree began to bear fruit.
